SEQ 377 R0 (Tony): a DEPTH GUARD on a declared global counter, bumped at every entry and capped at 50 -- the interpreted
depth of f(4) / g(4) is 5. Past the cap the body sets rsTrip and returns -7, the named sentinel. Why: once a compare's
and a binary's result stopped riding on the argument node (SEQ 376 R2, jit-compare-result), the folded `argument == 0`
no longer read true by accident, and the self-call still bakes its argument (the literal 4) at every depth, so the
recursion never bottoms out. The guard trips on the jit road until the argument slot lands (SEQ 376 R1c); on the
interpreted road it reads 5 and never trips -- the twin run after the jitted half says so.
